// Title: Hidden Powershell in Link File Pattern
// Sigma ID: 30e92f50-bb5a-4884-98b5-d20aa80f3d7a
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-02-06 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059.001
// Description: Detects events that appear when a user click on a link file with a powershell command in it
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate commands in .lnk files
// References:
//   - https://www.x86matthew.com/view_post?id=embed_exe_lnk
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_susp_embed_exe_lnk.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath =~ "C:\\Windows\\explorer.exe" and FolderPath =~ "C:\\Windows\\System32\\cmd.exe" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "powershell" and ProcessCommandLine contains ".lnk")
